      "writtenOn": "2021-06-15T18:36:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "why does this have to be qualified by !tpm_reset_in_progress() ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 116,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 116,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "2ff6d333a9bd06ddf0ed68509315896b7f644e35",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5b781e1c_9cdd74ea",
        "filename": "board/cr50/ap_state.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 116,
      "author": {
        "id": 1136059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-06-15T18:52:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh right I was going to ask what we should do about this.\n\nSome systems pulse TPM_RST_L twice when they reset. If we clear the ap ro verification state while TPM_RST_L is being debounced, then cr50 will never keep the AP RO verification state on these systems. It\u0027ll get cleared immediately during the second pulse.\n\nDo you think this is reasonable? We can also discuss this on the bug.",
      "parentUuid": "1301cf63_edcb4986",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 116,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 116,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "2ff6d333a9bd06ddf0ed68509315896b7f644e35",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "92aea11c_14a20e58",
        "filename": "board/cr50/ap_state.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 116,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-06-15T19:33:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "yes, protecting from dual pulse is necessary, but maybe it makes more sense to invoke ap_ro_device_reset() from the debounced TPM reset code?",
      "parentUuid": "5b781e1c_9cdd74ea",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 116,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 116,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "2ff6d333a9bd06ddf0ed68509315896b7f644e35",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "884e5be5_e0c08264",
        "filename": "board/cr50/ap_state.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 116,
      "author": {
        "id": 1136059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-06-16T16:42:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We need to clear this on the falling edge of TPM_RST_L. The TPM reset code happens on the rising edge.\n\nIf we clear it on the rising edge, it\u0027ll get cleared immediately when cr50 releases EC_RST_L after verifying RO.\n\ntpm_rst_asserted is the only code we have that runs on the falling edge.",
      "parentUuid": "92aea11c_14a20e58",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 116,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 116,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "2ff6d333a9bd06ddf0ed68509315896b7f644e35",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0101adc6_e77eaeb1",
        "filename": "board/cr50/ap_state.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 116,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-06-16T23:35:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "why does it have to be cleared on the falling edge of TPM_RST_L? The AP does not start communicating until TPM_RST_L is deasserted.\n\nI am just a bit concerned that we might skip calling ap_ro_device_reset() for whatever reason, this is it seems more reliable to me to always call ti when TPM reset programming is completing.",
      "parentUuid": "884e5be5_e0c08264",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 116,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 116,
        "endChar": 20
      },
